      "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <math.h>\n\n#define N_ITER 10 // number of simulation iterations\n#define DT 0.01f // time step\n#define SOFTENING 1e-9f // to avoid zero divisors\n\n/*\n * Each body holds coordinate positions (i.e., x, y, and z) and\n * velocities (i.e., vx, vy, and vz).\n */\ntypedef struct { float x, y, z, vx, vy, vz; } Body;\n\n/*\n * Compute the gravitational impact among all pairs of bodies in \n * the system.  The body data is supplied as separate arrays (SoA)\n * to improve cache locality during the O(n^2) pair loop.\n */\nvoid body_force(const float *restrict x,\n                const float *restrict y,\n                const float *restrict z,\n                float *restrict vx,\n                float *restrict vy,\n                float *restrict vz,\n                float dt, int n) {\n  /* Cache-block the i-loop: process TILE bodies at a time. */\n  const int TILE = 64;\n#pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\n  for (int ib = 0; ib < n; ib += TILE) {\n    int imax = ib + TILE;\n    if (imax > n) imax = n;\n\n    /* Preload this tile's positions into local arrays. */\n    float xi[TILE], yi[TILE], zi[TILE];\n    for (int i = ib; i < imax; ++i) {\n      int idx = i - ib;\n      xi[idx] = x[i];\n      yi[idx] = y[i];\n      zi[idx] = z[i];\n    }\n\n    float fx[TILE] = {0.0f};\n    float fy[TILE] = {0.0f};\n    float fz[TILE] = {0.0f};\n\n    /* For each j, update all bodies in this tile. */\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n      float xj = x[j];\n      float yj = y[j];\n      float zj = z[j];\n\n      for (int i = ib; i < imax; ++i) {\n        int idx = i - ib;\n        float dx = xj - xi[idx];\n        float dy = yj - yi[idx];\n        float dz = zj - zi[idx];\n        float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\n        float inv_dist = 1 / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\n        float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\n\n        fx[idx] += dx * inv_dist3; \n        fy[idx] += dy * inv_dist3; \n        fz[idx] += dz * inv_dist3;\n      }\n    }\n\n    for (int i = ib; i < imax; ++i) {\n      int idx = i - ib;\n      vx[i] += dt*fx[idx]; \n      vy[i] += dt*fy[idx]; \n      vz[i] += dt*fz[idx];\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n/*\n * Read a binary dataset with initilized bodies.\n */\nBody* read_dataset(int *nbodies) {\n  int b = fread(nbodies, sizeof(*nbodies), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading nbodie value\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n  Body *bodies = (Body *)malloc(*nbodies * sizeof(Body));\n  b = fread(bodies, *nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading input values\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n\n  return bodies;\n}\n\n/*\n * Write simulation results into a binary dataset.\n */\nvoid write_dataset(const int nbodies, Body *bodies) {\n  int b = fwrite(bodies, nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdout);\n  if (b != 1) {\n    fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError writing to output\\n\");\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n  }\n}\n\nint main(int argc,char **argv) {\n  int nbodies;\n\n  Body *bodies = read_dataset(&nbodies);\n\n  /* Convert the input AoS layout to separate arrays (SoA). */\n  float *x = malloc(nbodies * sizeof(float));\n  float *y = malloc(nbodies * sizeof(float));\n  float *z = malloc(nbodies * sizeof(float));\n  float *vx = malloc(nbodies * sizeof(float));\n  float *vy = malloc(nbodies * sizeof(float));\n  float *vz = malloc(nbodies * sizeof(float));\n\n  for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n    x[i] = bodies[i].x;\n    y[i] = bodies[i].y;\n    z[i] = bodies[i].z;\n    vx[i] = bodies[i].vx;\n    vy[i] = bodies[i].vy;\n    vz[i] = bodies[i].vz;\n  }\n\n  /*\n   * At each simulation iteration, interbody forces are computed,\n   * and bodies' positions are integrated.\n   */\n  for (int iter = 0; iter < N_ITER; iter++) {\n    body_force(x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, DT, nbodies);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; i++) {\n      x[i] += vx[i] * DT;\n      y[i] += vy[i] * DT;\n      z[i] += vz[i] * DT;\n    }\n  }\n\n  /* Convert back to the required AoS output layout. */\n  for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n    bodies[i].x = x[i];\n    bodies[i].y = y[i];\n    bodies[i].z = z[i];\n    bodies[i].vx = vx[i];\n    bodies[i].vy = vy[i];\n    bodies[i].vz = vz[i];\n  }\n\n  write_dataset(nbodies, bodies);\n\n  free(x); free(y); free(z); free(vx); free(vy); free(vz);\n  free(bodies);\n  \n  exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);\n}\n",
      "path": "src/nbody.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Cache-blocking the i-loop into tiles of 64 bodies, preloading each tile's positions into local arrays, and parallelizing over tiles reduces main-memory traffic from O(n^2) to O(n^2/TILE) while preserving the exact per-body j-summation order. This improves memory locality beyond the previous SoA+OpenMP version.",
  "notes": "The inner loop still accumulates forces in increasing j order for every body, so floating-point results remain bit-identical to the reference. Each tile's positions are read once from main memory and reused across all n iterations of the j-loop; the j arrays are streamed sequentially per tile, improving cache utilization.",
  "sources_kept": [],
  "transformations": [
    "Cache blocking over i-loop with TILE=64",
    "Preload tile positions into local arrays (xi/yi/zi)",
    "OpenMP parallelization moved from i-loop to tile loop"
  ]
